course: dictionary
lesson: 1653
title: Chinese: place, people or language
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word chinese can do three jobs. It can describe something, as in «Chinese food», which is food from China. It can name a language, such as Mandarin, the main kind of Chinese spoken in China. It can also name people: the Chinese are the people of China. Look at the words around it to see which job it is doing.
explain: Read this: «In Chinese names the family name comes first: in "Wang Lei", Wang is the surname.» Here Chinese describes names, so it means from China or about China. Ask: what word would fit here? Try swapping in "from China" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Capital letters give a clue too. In English, Chinese always starts with a capital letter, because it names a country, a people or a language. Words like «Chinese restaurants» and «Chinese New Year» use the same capital letter, so you can spot the name of a place or group.
fact: Chinese means from China or about China.
fact: Chinese is also the name of the language spoken in China; Mandarin is its main kind.
fact: The Chinese are the people of China.
fact: «The Chinese printed books with carved wooden blocks over 1,100 years ago.»
fact: «Kowtow» comes from Chinese for "knock head", a deep bow touching the forehead to the ground.
exercise: Nadia eats «Chinese food» at a restaurant. What does Chinese mean here? | *From China | The name of a school | A language in Italy | A kind of chopstick
exercise: «She is learning Chinese at school.» What is Chinese in this sentence? | *The language spoken in China | The people of China only | A long wall | A kind of food
exercise: «The Chinese printed books with carved wooden blocks over 1,100 years ago.» Who printed the books? | *The Chinese people | Ukrainian folk singers | Western pop stars | A famous emperor's grandson
test: «Kowtow» comes from Chinese for "knock head". What is a kowtow? | *A deep bow, with the forehead touching the ground | A loud shout | A type of noodle | A carved wooden block
test: Singing styles differ around the world: Chinese folk and opera singing, Ukrainian folk singing and Western pop. Which one is Chinese? | Western pop | Ukrainian folk singing | *Chinese opera singing
exam: In «Chinese restaurants», what kind of word is Chinese? | A verb, because it shows an action | A full stop | A noun, the name of a language | *An adjective, because it describes the restaurants
